{"id": "EUVD-2021-34884", "enisaUuid": "9dfde35c-c034-3739-a5a3-882fbeba1763", "description": "Servor 1.0.0 through 4.0.2 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to escape the served root by sending URL-encoded dot segments. Attackers can send %2e%2e/ sequences, which decodeURI() decodes before path.join() in serveStaticFile and serveDirectoryListing, to read arbitrary files and list directories outside the root.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:46:58", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/lukejacksonn/servor/pull/70", "https://github.com/lukejacksonn/servor/commit/ec7d824ea6903c0fb97a452045bbb8335198cbab", "https://github.com/lukejacksonn/servor", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/servor-1.0.0-through-4.0.2-unauthenticated-path-traversal-via-url-encoded-dot-segments"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pcvv-rm69-6cv3", "CVE-2021-48011"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.56, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c46bab03-9db2-3b35-b0a4-74b18c42d266", "product": {"name": "servor", "vendor": {"name": "lukejacksonn"}}, "product_version": "1.0.0 \u22644.0.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8a8787ef-7890-351d-9b5c-f8a344b8c09c", "vendor": {"name": "lukejacksonn"}}], "isExploited": false}